codex
The observed cause is precise: validation stores the declared value in `__dict__` (`x=1`) and the duplicate name in `__pydantic_extra__` (`x=2`); the core serializer merges extras after fields, so the latter wins. I’m choosing a collision-only shallow serialization copy with conflicting extras removed. This preserves field serializers, JSON mode, include/exclude behavior, and alias selection without mutating the model. I rejected replacing the dumped value from `__dict__`, because that would bypass Pydantic’s serialization logic.
